WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.960
What do companies in e-commerce, entertainment, healthcare, manufacturing, marketing, finance,

2
00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:13.560
tech, and hundreds of other industries all have in common?

3
00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:17.600
You guessed it, they all use data.

4
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:23.399
Organizations of all kinds need data analysts to help them improve their processes, identify

5
00:00:23.399 --> 00:00:29.940
opportunities and trends, launch new products, provide great customer service, and make thoughtful

6
00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:30.940
decisions.

7
00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:36.139
Hi, I'm Tony, a program manager at Google, and a data analyst myself.

8
00:00:36.139 --> 00:00:39.939
I'd like to welcome you to the Google Data Analytics Certificate.

9
00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:44.740
Now, there are lots of great reasons to earn this certificate.

10
00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:49.299
Maybe you're thinking about starting a career in the exciting world of data analytics.

11
00:00:49.299 --> 00:00:53.959
Or maybe you're just fascinated by the power of data as I am.

12
00:00:53.959 --> 00:00:58.220
No matter what brought you here, you're in the right place to kickstart a career and

13
00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:03.000
learn industry-relevant skills in data analytics.

14
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.599
But first, what exactly is data?

15
00:01:05.599 --> 00:01:09.480
Well, I like to say that data is a collection of facts.

16
00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:15.559
This collection can include numbers, pictures, videos, words, measurements, observations,

17
00:01:15.559 --> 00:01:17.000
and more.

18
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.739
Once you have data, analytics puts it to work through analysis.

19
00:01:21.739 --> 00:01:27.959
Data analysis is the collection, transformation, and organization of data in order to draw

20
00:01:27.959 --> 00:01:32.940
conclusions, make predictions, and drive informed decision making.

21
00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:35.220
And it doesn't stop there.

22
00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:41.319
Data evolves over time, which means this analysis, or analytics as we call it, can give us new

23
00:01:41.319 --> 00:01:45.800
information throughout data's entire lifecycle.

24
00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:47.540
Data is everywhere.

25
00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:50.300
You use and create data every day.

26
00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:55.339
Have you ever read reviews of a product before deciding whether or not to buy it?

27
00:01:55.339 --> 00:01:57.400
That's data analysis.

28
00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:01.980
Or maybe you wear a fitness tracker to count your steps so you can stay active throughout

29
00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:02.980
the day.

30
00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:03.980
That's data analysis.

31
00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:11.059
But you don't just use data, you also create huge amounts of it every single day.

32
00:02:11.059 --> 00:02:18.139
Anytime you use your phone, look up something online, stream music, shop with a credit card,

33
00:02:18.139 --> 00:02:24.059
post on social media, or use GPS to map a route, you're creating data.

34
00:02:24.059 --> 00:02:28.699
Our digital world and the millions of smart devices inside of it have made the amount

35
00:02:28.699 --> 00:02:32.660
of data available truly mind-blowing.

36
00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:38.179
Here at Google, we process more than 40,000 searches every second.

37
00:02:38.179 --> 00:02:44.779
That's 3.5 billion searches a day and 1.2 trillion searches every year.

38
00:02:44.779 --> 00:02:47.460
Here's another way to think about it.

39
00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:50.300
YouTube has almost 2 billion users.

40
00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:54.940
If YouTube users made up a country, it would be the largest in the world.

41
00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:58.300
All of that data is transforming the world around us.

42
00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:05.059
The publication, The Economist, recently called data the world's most valuable resource.

43
00:03:05.059 --> 00:03:10.160
So it's easy to see why data analysts are so valued by their organizations.

44
00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:13.419
And what exactly does a data analyst do?

45
00:03:13.419 --> 00:03:19.699
Put simply, a data analyst is someone who collects, transforms, and organizes data in

46
00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:22.339
order to help make informed decisions.

47
00:03:22.339 --> 00:03:27.320
Besides the role itself, one of the most exciting parts of being a data analyst is the number

48
00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:29.619
of opportunities available.

49
00:03:29.619 --> 00:03:34.339
The demand for data analysts is greater than the number of qualified people to fill these

50
00:03:34.339 --> 00:03:35.940
job openings.

51
00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:41.779
And this certificate program is a great first step in your journey to finding a job you

52
00:03:41.779 --> 00:03:42.779
love.

53
00:03:42.779 --> 00:03:48.240
Data analysts come from many different backgrounds and have all kinds of life experiences.

54
00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:54.160
You don't need decades of work experience or an expensive education to get started.

55
00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:59.520
Many data analysts taught themselves the skills they needed to land their first job, just

56
00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:01.880
like you're doing right now.

57
00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:06.479
Okay, now let's talk more about what you're going to learn.

58
00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:11.880
The Google Data Analytics Certificate is split into courses based on different processes

59
00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:13.919
for data analysis.

60
00:04:13.919 --> 00:04:21.279
Those are Ask, Prepare, Process, Analyze, Share, and Act.

61
00:04:21.279 --> 00:04:24.160
Plan to watch these videos in order.

62
00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:29.640
Each one covers a new topic, and every topic builds on what you've learned before, making

63
00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:32.440
it easy to track your progress.

64
00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:35.000
And you're in the driver's seat.

65
00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:40.399
Even though you might see things organized by weeks, everything can be completed at your

66
00:04:40.399 --> 00:04:41.760
own pace.

67
00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:45.279
So you decide how much you want to do each day.

68
00:04:45.279 --> 00:04:50.260
By the end of the program, you'll take everything you've learned and turn it into a project

69
00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:56.480
that you can use to show off your skills and wow hiring managers at your job interviews.

70
00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:59.760
Now along the way, you'll also hear from Googlers.

71
00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:02.720
That's what we call people who work here at Google.

72
00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:07.880
They'll give you an inside look at what it's like to work in our industry and share personal

73
00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:10.920
